WEBVTT


00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:01.040
Now it is time for you to call

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.480
some tips for an online raffle

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.880
as a professional.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.040
First tip,

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:07.800
focus on one raffle at a time.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.320
This may be very obvious what I am saying,

00:00:09.321 --> 00:00:10.641
but it is always better to lend

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.240
attention to one event than to several.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:12.616
Also, 

00:00:12.616 --> 00:00:14.240
if you have several raffles at the same time,

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.160
you can make your own followers confused.

00:00:16.279 --> 00:00:17.080
Second advice,

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.400
choose an award that is striking.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.880
This will help more people sign up and make

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.840
other participants join the event.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:23.680
Third board,

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.000
organizes test raffles to fine-tune details.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.160
Checking this with your close circle,

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:28.920
you will be able to

00:00:28.921 --> 00:00:31.161
to know which formats are most attractive to users,

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.000
what awards you can offer

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.360
and which process will be best suited

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:36.440
to what you want to achieve.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.280
Fourth tip,

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.400
establishes the duration

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.120
and allocate the budget you will invest

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.480
to disseminate your dynamics.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:42.440
Study your market,

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.640
analyzes the results of other similar dynamics

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.280
and sets out the goal of overcoming them.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.019
5th tip, 

00:00:47.019 --> 00:00:48.120
measure results.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.600
After the storm comes the calm.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:51.360
the results you achieved,

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:52.181
for example, 

00:00:52.181 --> 00:00:53.880
the number of people who participated,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.240
the comments there were,

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.920
the reaction to the awards you offer.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.000
This will help you decide,

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:58.600
obviously, 

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.320
whether you organize another raffle or not.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.600
6th and final board,

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.240
you can get close to small influencers

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:05.520
to help you with the dissemination
